0 A vintage crawler display compares low, stepped and upright tracks plus two single-wheel wraps.
0 Name: TECHNIC_TREAD_CRAWLER-Constraints.ldr
0 Author: Holly Wood
0 Unofficial Model
0 // Scene: A small blue oval sits above a wider yellow loop. A brown loop climbs between unequal wheels on a tall brick support, while orange and black rings surround isolated wheels beside them.
0 // Rigid construction: 7049 bearing bricks with integral axle bushes carry older 7039, 715 and 35 wheel assemblies. Ordinary bricks raise and offset some wheel positions.
0 // Build lesson: A dedicated bearing brick and matching wheel pack can define a compact undercarriage. Learn the support interface before choosing the track outline or substituting newer wheels.
0 // Reuse: These old cylindrical-axle wheel assemblies are not generic modern cross-axle wheels. Single-wheel legacy routes generate tangent warnings; the display does not prove tread size, tension or a complete drivetrain.
0 ROTATION CENTER 0 0 0 1 "Custom" 
0 ROTATION CONFIG 0 0
